cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use PRCoords in published work, cite it as below.
title: PRCoords
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wang
    given-names: Mingye
    alias: Artoria2e5
    email: arthur200126@gmail.com
    website: https://github.com/Artoria2e5
  - family-names: Wang
    given-names: Dingyuan
    alias: gumblex
    email: gumblex@aosc.io
    website: https://github.com/gumblex
repository-code: https://github.com/Artoria2e5/PRCoords
url: https://github.com/Artoria2e5/PRCoords
license:
  - CC0-1.0
  - GPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - GCJ-02
  - BD-09
  - WGS-84
  - coordinate obfuscation
  - China
  - GIS
  - geodesy
abstract: >-
  PRCoords implements the Chinese coordinate obfuscation methods GCJ-02 and
  BD-09: forward transform WGS-84 -> GCJ-02 -> BD-09, plus one-step and
  iterative inverses. There are versions in Python, JavaScript and C/C++ (C
  ABI), PostgreSQL, and more.
references:
  - type: software-code
    title: EMQ Algorithm.Coords.Converter
    authors:
      - name: EMQ
    url: https://archive.is/20130815104734/emq.googlecode.com/svn/emq/src/Algorithm/Coords/Converter.java
    repository-code: https://github.com/Artoria2e5/emq/blob/master/emq/src/Algorithm/Coords/Converter.java
    notes: The original GCJ leak, from a Java demo project by a contractor.

  - type: software-code
    title: on4wp7 coordinate conversion
    authors:
      - name: on4wp7
    url: https://archive.is/20150702191259/https://on4wp7.codeplex.com/SourceControl/changeset/view/21483%23353936
    notes: Earliest rationalized forward GCJ implementation, 2013.

  - type: software-code
    title: ChinaMapShift
    authors:
      - name: anonymous
    url: https://gist.github.com/anonymous/e7c6f67555099180ce1ae8da4ba2c513
    notes: Quick iterative inverse for GCJ, 2014.

  - type: software-code
    title: pycoordtrans
    authors:
      - name: zxteloiv
    repository-code: https://github.com/zxteloiv/pycoordtrans
    notes: Source for the BD-09 offsets, 2014.

  - type: software
    title: eviltransform
    authors:
      - name: googollee
    repository-code: https://github.com/googollee/eviltransform
    notes: >-
      Popular cross-language take on the problem. Its parameters have been wrong
      since June 2016, especially for BD-09.

  - type: software-code
    title: EvilTransform.cs
    authors:
      - name: Leask
    repository-code: https://github.com/Leask/EvilTransform
    notes: Early refactor of the EMQ Java code, and where eviltransform got its name.

  - type: software
    title: geoChina
    authors:
      - name: caijun
    repository-code: https://github.com/caijun/geoChina
    notes: R implementation with the ChinaMapShift iterative inverse.

  - type: article
    title: "从地球到火星 ～ 论 GCJ-02 及其衍生"
    authors:
      - name: Ishisashi
    url: https://chaoli.club/index.php/4777/0
    notes: Writeup on this subject, with an enhanced version of the demo.

  - type: newspaper-article
    title: News report on the person who designed GCJ-02
    authors:
      - name: People's Daily Online
    url: https://archive.fo/20110804185923/http://cxzy.people.com.cn/GB/196034/14908095.html
    notes: In Chinese, archived 2011-08-04.

